"answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics through the use of AI algorithms. The project was introduced by Alex with Sarah Tan as the lead, starting with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. Emily called for ideas from R&D by July 20th to enhance data visualization tools. Tom shared initial findings suggesting a 20% efficiency increase, to be discussed on August 5th. The budget was later adjusted to $550,000 by Jordan due to unforeseen expenses, and subsequently approved at $2M by the executive board to cover all phases. A compliance plan budget of $55,000 was also allocated. The project is exploring partnerships with TechInnovate. Carlos announced the successful completion of the testing phase, with a celebration scheduled for October 10th. Additionally, a separate entity, Zenith Innovations, was onboarded for a 'Revolutionary AI Project' with an onboarding session on April 15th, 2023."
